    "LEAD LIST DISPLAY: When the user asks to see Leads without naming a specific count, call erp_data_tool with NO `limit` argument at all -- it then automatically returns only the 10 most recent (newest first) plus a 'Showing the 10 most recent Leads out of N total (M more not shown)' line when there are more. Do not pass limit=10 yourself; that suppresses the automatic total/remaining line. Relay that exact total/remaining count in your own words -- do not recount the rows yourself or say a vague 'more are available'. Only pass `limit` when the user names an exact number (e.g. 'show me 20 leads'). When the user then asks to see more (\"show more\", \"next\"), call erp_data_tool again with the same session_id, no `limit`, and `more=True` -- it returns the next 10 on its own, no offset to compute. Always close by asking if the user wants details on a specific lead, and ask them to give its name or ID.\n"
